```'}, {'BodyText': 'If returnChunkSize() happens to encounter an error it will return -1. Notice that the return value is not checked before the memcpy operation (CWE-252), so -1 can be passed as the size argument to memcpy() (CWE-805). Because memcpy() assumes that the value is unsigned, it will be interpreted as MAXINT-1 (CWE-195), and therefore will copy far more memory than is likely available to the destination buffer (CWE-787, CWE-788).'}]}, {'ID': 'DX-138', 'Entries': [{'IntroText': "This example shows a typical attempt to parse a string with an error resulting from a difference in assumptions between the caller to a function and the function's action."}, {'Nature': 'Bad', 'Language': 'C', 'ExampleCode': 'int proc_msg(char *s, int msg_len)
