```'}, {'BodyText': 'Assuming a string consisting of standard alpha-numeric characters, such as "Jane Smith", is submitted in the request the HTTP response including this cookie might take the following form:'}, {'Nature': 'Result', 'ExampleCode': '```
	HTTP/1.1 200 OK
	...
	Set-Cookie: author=Jane Smith
	...
```'}, {'BodyText': 'However, because the value of the cookie is composed of unvalidated user input, the response will only maintain this form if the value submitted for AUTHOR_PARAM does not contain any CR and LF characters. If an attacker submits a malicious string, such as'}, {'Nature': 'Attack', 'ExampleCode': '```
	Wiley Hacker\r\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n
```'}, {'BodyText': 'then the HTTP response would be split into two responses of the following form:'}, {'Nature': 'Result', 'ExampleCode': '```
