[{'ID': 'DX-214', 'Entries': [{'IntroText': 'The following code attempts to synchronize on an object, but does not execute anything in the synchronized block. This does not actually accomplish anything and may be a sign that a programmer is wrestling with synchronization but has not yet achieved the result they intend.'}, {'Nature': 'Bad', 'Language': 'Java', 'ExampleCode': '```
	synchronized(this) { }
```'}, {'BodyText': 'Instead, in a correct usage, the synchronized statement should contain procedures that access or modify data that is exposed to multiple threads. For example, consider a scenario in which several threads are accessing student records at the same time. The method which sets the student ID to a new value will need to make sure that nobody else is accessing this data at the same time and will require synchronization.'}, {'Nature': 'Good', 'ExampleCode': '```
	public void setID(int ID){
		synchronized(this){
			this.ID = ID;
		}
	}
```'}]}]

